<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Carlo I Tocco</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 1429</span> · <a href="/centuries/15th-century">15th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Carlo I Tocco was Count palatine of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kefalonia">Cephalonia</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zakynthos">Zakynthos</a> from about 1376 and Duke of Leucadia. He took <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ioannina">Ioannina</a> in 1411 and Arta in 1416, reuniting the Despotate of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/epirus">Epirus</a> under his rule, and received the title of despot from the Byzantine emperor. After his death the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ottoman-empire">Ottomans</a> took Ioannina in 1430.</p></div>
